{title: Gracious and Holy}
{artist: C. Michael Pilato}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 90}

Verse 1
[Em]You made the [Gm]Earth and the [F]heavens.
[Em]Spoke words to [Gm]form them and [F]fill them.
[Em]So all that we [Gm]have is by [F]Your hand.
[Gm]Gracious and [F/A]holy You [Em/Bm]are.
[Em]You gave us [Gm]freedom and [F]purpose.
[Em]We chose rebellion [Gm]and [F]curses.
[Em]But hope lingered [Gm]under the [F]surface.
[Gm]Gracious and [F/A]holy You [Em/Bm]are.
[Gm]Gracious and [F/A]holy You [Bm]are.

Verse 2
You are [Em]here, always with [Gm]me,
Nearer than [Bm]sacred to naked should [F/A]be.
You speak [Em]promises over my [Gm]shame.
[Bm]I know that [Cm]I'll never [F]be the [Bm]same.

Verse 3
[Em]You came to dwell with Your people;
Strengthen the downcast and feeble;
And rescue us from every evil.
Gracious and holy You are.
Humbly you gave Your life for us.
Hope is reversing our curses,
Restoring our freedom and purpose.
Gracious and holy You are.
Gracious and holy You are.

Verse 4
You are [Em]here, always with [Gm]me.
Nearer than [Bm]righteous to wretched should [F/A]be.
You speak [Em]promises over my [Gm]shame.
[Bm]I know that [Cm]I'll never [F]be the [Bm]same.

Verse 5
Now you are [Gm]seated in [F]Heaven,
[Em]So, by the [Gm]Spirit You've [F]given,
[Em]We will proclaim, "[Gm]Christ is [F]risen!"
[Gm]Gracious and [F/A]holy You [Em/Bm]are.
[Gm]Gracious and [F/A]holy You [Bm]are.

Verse 6
You are [Em]here, always with [Gm]me,
Nearer forever [Bm]than failure could [F/A]be.
You poured [Em]righteousness over my [Gm]shame.
Called me Your [Bm]child and then gave me Your [F/A]name.
You are [Em]here, always with [Gm]me,
Nearer forever [Bm]than failure could [F/A]be.
You poured [Em]righteousness over my [Gm]shame.
[Bm]I know that [Cm]I'll never [F]be the [Bm]same.
[Gm]I know that [Cm]I'll never [F]be the [Bm]same.
